  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FREE EDUCATION PROJECT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is a partnership between the World Bank, EU, UK and Ireland and Ministry of Basic and Senior Secondary Education (MBSSE). The goal of the project is to improve the management of the education system, teaching practices, and learning conditions. The project is financed through a World Bank IDA grant of $50M and $15.97M from a Multi Donor Trust Fund (MDTF) with contributions from Ireland, UK and EU. Government of Sierra Leone is in the process of securing additional IDA funds of US$40 million to support school feeding, school health, and teaching and learning materials for accelerating foundational learning and to expand project activities to reach more beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
